{"schema_version":"M2D-ATOM-1.1.0","topic_id":"PHY-M2D-RM-20260915","source_id":"SYN-M2D-20260915-V1","source_corpus_sha256":"6aac1841445e051244c3ad41f2d1ccab0d21e486b92efd0da68a87298bb29648","created_at":"2026-09-15","contract_revisions":{"physics_pr350_head_initial_read":"88e7adaac2368bd65dc98537b892e6fae8836994","physics_pr350_intermediate_head":"96a6dcec170d73eafe0b8a12af1daca1c51634e2","physics_pr350_head":"f8c606599d3c2061c968f377dea79b7ab868bbe8","v3b_pr364_head":"6be71db1a321c449131a26ee3084b6b9c0edca28","physics_core_contract_version":"1.1.0","core_contract_blob":"291d42c8999205c6c08660525f262fde0e5d34c1","packet_contract_blob":"e84c6e23bf2bba01426f2b5a95c9fa99084b7519","topic_workflow_blob":"b968c118cad27ca8e11b9ffe4608a00c539a98b9","canonical_workbench_blob":"4a149fbc48c5a32d147f5a094126277c74482c9b","applicable_v3_gate_blobs":{"PHY-M2D-SHARED-CLOCK.v3.json":"af715733f1a28b52395f871a5ab5d78c136d3e2a","PHY-VEC-COMPONENTS.v3.json":"aaf4c667056a44915a5a0a71d34a19f8a7ee37c5","PHY-VEC-ADD-SUB.v3.json":"fa504ad7e9bc5c46c10ee0aad833489606bf9ea5"}},"buckets":[{"bucket_id":"B01","subtopic":"Observer, frame, axes, origin and common clock","intrinsic_badge":"Easy","badge_change":"RETAINED","reason":"Validated against actual reasoning demand; no change from proposed badge."},{"bucket_id":"B02","subtopic":"Path, distance, displacement and average quantities","intrinsic_badge":"Medium","badge_change":"RETAINED","reason":"Validated against actual reasoning demand; no change from proposed badge."},{"bucket_id":"B03","subtopic":"Coordinates, components and reconstructing a vector visually","intrinsic_badge":"Hard","badge_change":"RETAINED","reason":"Validated against actual reasoning demand; no change from proposed badge."},{"bucket_id":"B04","subtopic":"Constant motion in two coordinates; tables and graphs","intrinsic_badge":"Medium","badge_change":"RETAINED","reason":"Validated against actual reasoning demand; no change from proposed badge."},{"bucket_id":"B05","subtopic":"One-dimensional relative motion, units and signs","intrinsic_badge":"Medium","badge_change":"RETAINED","reason":"Validated against actual reasoning demand; no change from proposed badge."},{"bucket_id":"B06","subtopic":"Relative velocity in two dimensions and observer reversal","intrinsic_badge":"Hard","badge_change":"RETAINED","reason":"Validated against actual reasoning demand; no change from proposed badge."},{"bucket_id":"B07","subtopic":"Meeting requires the same position at the same time","intrinsic_badge":"Hard","badge_change":"RETAINED","reason":"Validated against actual reasoning demand; no change from proposed badge."},{"bucket_id":"B08","subtopic":"Boat/current and rain/observer model transfer; ambiguity","intrinsic_badge":"Hard","badge_change":"RETAINED","reason":"Validated against actual reasoning demand; no change from proposed badge."}],"atoms":[{"atom_id":"SRC-CONV-001","kind":"source_condition","text":"Ground frame is used unless stated otherwise.","bucket":"B01","source_ref":"SYN-M2D-20260915-V1","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-CONV-002","kind":"source_condition","text":"+x is east and +y is north.","bucket":"B01","source_ref":"SYN-M2D-20260915-V1","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-CONV-003","kind":"source_condition","text":"Positions are in metres and times are in seconds unless stated otherwise.","bucket":"B01","source_ref":"SYN-M2D-20260915-V1","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-CONV-004","kind":"source_condition","text":"Velocities are constant over the interval described.","bucket":"B04","source_ref":"SYN-M2D-20260915-V1","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-CONV-005","kind":"source_condition","text":"A and B in collision questions are point objects.","bucket":"B07","source_ref":"SYN-M2D-20260915-V1","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-CONV-006","kind":"source_condition","text":"Simultaneous start means a shared t = 0.","bucket":"B07","source_ref":"SYN-M2D-20260915-V1","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-CONV-007","kind":"source_condition","text":"Parenthesized ordered pairs give x and y components.","bucket":"B03","source_ref":"SYN-M2D-20260915-V1","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B01-01","kind":"contract_concept","text":"A motion description needs a named observer/reference frame.","bucket":"B01","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B01-02","kind":"contract_concept","text":"Axes, positive directions and origin are conventions; changing them changes component signs but not the physical motion.","bucket":"B01","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B01-03","kind":"contract_concept","text":"Objects compared in one calculation must use a common clock when simultaneity matters.","bucket":"B01","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B02-01","kind":"contract_concept","text":"Distance is total path length; displacement is final position minus initial position.","bucket":"B02","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B02-02","kind":"contract_concept","text":"Average speed is total distance divided by total elapsed time; average velocity uses displacement over the same elapsed time.","bucket":"B02","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B02-03","kind":"contract_concept","text":"A vector magnitude is not one of its signed components.","bucket":"B02","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B03-01","kind":"contract_concept","text":"Two-coordinate change is computed component-by-component: final minus initial.","bucket":"B03","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B03-02","kind":"contract_concept","text":"Perpendicular components can be reconstructed as one arrow using a right triangle and Pythagoras.","bucket":"B03","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B03-03","kind":"contract_concept","text":"A negative component indicates direction along a chosen axis; it does not make speed negative.","bucket":"B03","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B04-01","kind":"contract_concept","text":"For constant planar velocity, x and y evolve separately but share the same elapsed time.","bucket":"B04","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B04-02","kind":"contract_concept","text":"A coordinate table and x(t), y(t) graphs are alternate representations of the same motion.","bucket":"B04","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B04-03","kind":"contract_concept","text":"A flat position-time segment means zero component velocity during that interval.","bucket":"B04","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B05-01","kind":"contract_concept","text":"Relative velocity in one dimension follows target minus observer with signs set by the chosen axis.","bucket":"B05","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B05-02","kind":"contract_concept","text":"Reversing target and observer reverses the relative-velocity sign/direction but not its magnitude.","bucket":"B05","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B05-03","kind":"contract_concept","text":"Equal velocities imply zero relative velocity and therefore constant separation, not automatic co-location.","bucket":"B05","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B05-04","kind":"contract_concept","text":"Units must be made consistent before relative-velocity subtraction.","bucket":"B05","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B06-01","kind":"contract_concept","text":"Two-dimensional relative velocity is found by subtracting corresponding components in the same order.","bucket":"B06","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B06-02","kind":"contract_concept","text":"Observer reversal negates every relative-velocity component and leaves the magnitude unchanged.","bucket":"B06","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B06-03","kind":"contract_concept","text":"Relative position uses the same ordering as relative velocity, and its initial value need not be zero.","bucket":"B06","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B07-01","kind":"contract_concept","text":"A meeting/collision requires x positions equal and y positions equal at one same admissible time.","bucket":"B07","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B07-02","kind":"contract_concept","text":"Intersecting geometric paths do not prove collision because arrival times may differ.","bucket":"B07","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B07-03","kind":"contract_concept","text":"A positive-control meeting case is needed so 'no collision' cannot succeed as a universal strategy.","bucket":"B07","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B08-01","kind":"contract_concept","text":"Boat velocity relative to ground equals boat relative to water plus water relative to ground, with frames named.","bucket":"B08","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B08-02","kind":"contract_concept","text":"River crossing time is determined by the across-river component, not automatically by resultant ground speed.","bucket":"B08","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B08-03","kind":"contract_concept","text":"Rain relative to an observer is rain-ground minus observer-ground; apparent horizontal motion can arise even when ground-frame rain has zero horizontal component.","bucket":"B08","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B08-04","kind":"contract_concept","text":"Ambiguous relative-motion prompts must identify missing direction/frame information rather than invent it.","bucket":"B08","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-C-B08-05","kind":"contract_concept","text":"Closest approach is enrichment: compare squared separation using a table or complete a square, without calculus.","bucket":"B08","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-EQ-001","kind":"equation","text":"Δx = x_f − x_i; Δy = y_f − y_i","bucket":"B03","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-EQ-002","kind":"equation","text":"|Δr| = √(Δx²+Δy²)","bucket":"B03","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-EQ-003","kind":"equation","text":"v_avg,x=Δx/Δt; v_avg,y=Δy/Δt","bucket":"B02","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-EQ-004","kind":"equation","text":"x=x0+v_x t; y=y0+v_y t","bucket":"B04","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-EQ-005","kind":"equation","text":"v_A/B=v_A/G−v_B/G","bucket":"B05","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-EQ-006","kind":"equation","text":"r_A/B=r_A/G−r_B/G; r_A/B(t)=r_A/B(0)+v_A/B t","bucket":"B06","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-EQ-007","kind":"equation","text":"x_A(t)=x_B(t) AND y_A(t)=y_B(t) at one admissible t","bucket":"B07","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-EQ-008","kind":"equation","text":"v_B/G=v_B/W+v_W/G","bucket":"B08","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-EQ-009","kind":"equation","text":"|v|=√(v_x²+v_y²)","bucket":"B03","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-EQ-010","kind":"equation","text":"speed(m/s)=speed(km/h)×5/18","bucket":"B05","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-EQ-011","kind":"equation","text":"d²(t)=Δx(t)²+Δy(t)²","bucket":"B08","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"REQ-VIS-001","kind":"visual_relationship","text":"Path/displacement diagram: two-leg path and direct displacement arrow must be visually distinguishable.","bucket":"B02","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":"diagrams/path-displacement.svg"},{"atom_id":"REQ-VIS-002","kind":"visual_relationship","text":"Vector component triangle: horizontal and vertical components form perpendicular legs and resultant is the hypotenuse.","bucket":"B03","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":"diagrams/component-triangle.svg"},{"atom_id":"REQ-VIS-003","kind":"visual_relationship","text":"Time-labelled planar path: recorded positions carry time labels and stationary interval is visible.","bucket":"B04","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":"diagrams/time-labelled-path.svg"},{"atom_id":"REQ-VIS-004","kind":"visual_relationship","text":"x(t)/y(t) graphs: both use time on horizontal axes with a shared time convention.","bucket":"B04","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":"diagrams/xy-time-graphs.svg"},{"atom_id":"REQ-VIS-005","kind":"visual_relationship","text":"Relative-velocity subtraction construction: target, observer and target-relative-observer arrows obey the subtraction/addition triangle.","bucket":"B06","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":"diagrams/relative-subtraction.svg"},{"atom_id":"REQ-VIS-006","kind":"visual_relationship","text":"Collision/non-collision pair: same geometric crossing point but one case shares arrival time and the other does not.","bucket":"B07","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":"diagrams/collision-pair.svg"},{"atom_id":"REQ-VIS-007","kind":"visual_relationship","text":"Boat-frame diagram: boat/water, water/ground and boat/ground arrows form a frame-labelled vector sum.","bucket":"B08","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":"diagrams/boat-current.svg"},{"atom_id":"REQ-VIS-008","kind":"visual_relationship","text":"Rain-frame diagram: ground rain arrow, observer ground arrow and rain/observer relative arrow are frame-labelled.","bucket":"B08","source_ref":"ASSIGNMENT-CONTRACT","required":true,"notes":"diagrams/rain-observer.svg"},{"atom_id":"RES-001","kind":"research_support","text":"OpenStax University Physics 4.1 supports coordinate-system setup, displacement as final minus initial position, average velocity in multiple dimensions, and independence of perpendicular components.","bucket":"B03","source_ref":"WEB-AUTHORITY","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"RES-002","kind":"research_support","text":"OpenStax University Physics 4.5 supports named reference frames, relative position/velocity vector equations and one/two-dimensional relative motion diagrams.","bucket":"B06","source_ref":"WEB-AUTHORITY","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"RES-003","kind":"research_support","text":"OpenStax Physics 2.3 supports position-time graph conventions and slope as average velocity for straight-line graph segments.","bucket":"B04","source_ref":"WEB-AUTHORITY","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"RES-004","kind":"research_support","text":"NIST SI definitions support metre (m) for length and second (s) for time; this run uses derived m/s consistently.","bucket":"B05","source_ref":"WEB-AUTHORITY","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q01-FULL","kind":"source_question_full","text":"A learner walks 6 m east and then 8 m north in a total of 14 s. (a) Draw the path and displacement. (b) Find distance and displacement magnitude. (c) Find average speed. (d) Give average velocity as east/north components and its magnitude. Explain why average speed and the magnitude of average velocity differ here.","bucket":"B02","source_ref":"Q01","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q01-D01","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"6 m east first leg","bucket":"B02","source_ref":"Q01","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q01-D02","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"8 m north second leg","bucket":"B02","source_ref":"Q01","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q01-D03","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"total elapsed time 14 s","bucket":"B02","source_ref":"Q01","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q01-SP01","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Draw the path and displacement.","bucket":"B02","source_ref":"Q01","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q01-SP02","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Find distance and displacement magnitude.","bucket":"B02","source_ref":"Q01","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q01-SP03","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Find average speed.","bucket":"B02","source_ref":"Q01","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q01-SP04","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Give average velocity components/magnitude and explain the difference.","bucket":"B02","source_ref":"Q01","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q02-FULL","kind":"source_question_full","text":"A tracked object has positions shown below. It moves along a straight line at constant velocity between successive recorded points. (a) Draw its path with time labels. (b) Find the velocity components in 0–4 s and in 4–6 s. (c) Find total distance, displacement components and average velocity over 0–6 s. (d) A student says, “The object moved at 5 m/s for all 6 s.” Diagnose the claim.\n\n| t (s) | x (m) | y (m) |\n|---:|---:|---:|\n| 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| 2 | 6 | 8 |\n| 4 | 12 | 16 |\n| 6 | 12 | 16 |","bucket":"B04","source_ref":"Q02","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q02-D01","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"(t,x,y)=(0,0,0)","bucket":"B04","source_ref":"Q02","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q02-D02","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"(2,6,8)","bucket":"B04","source_ref":"Q02","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q02-D03","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"(4,12,16)","bucket":"B04","source_ref":"Q02","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q02-D04","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"(6,12,16)","bucket":"B04","source_ref":"Q02","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q02-D05","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"straight line at constant velocity between successive recorded points","bucket":"B04","source_ref":"Q02","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q02-SP01","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Draw path with time labels.","bucket":"B04","source_ref":"Q02","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q02-SP02","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Find velocity components in 0–4 s and 4–6 s.","bucket":"B04","source_ref":"Q02","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q02-SP03","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Find total distance, displacement components and average velocity over 0–6 s.","bucket":"B04","source_ref":"Q02","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q02-SP04","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Diagnose the 5 m/s-for-all-6-s claim.","bucket":"B04","source_ref":"Q02","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q03-FULL","kind":"source_question_full","text":"At t = 0 an object is at (2, 5) m. Its velocity is (3, −4) m/s. (a) Find its position at t = 6 s. (b) Find its displacement components and distance travelled in those 6 s. (c) Sketch the starting point, ending point and velocity direction. Explain the negative component without calling speed negative.","bucket":"B03","source_ref":"Q03","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q03-D01","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"initial position (2,5) m","bucket":"B03","source_ref":"Q03","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q03-D02","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"velocity (3,-4) m/s","bucket":"B03","source_ref":"Q03","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q03-D03","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"elapsed time 6 s","bucket":"B03","source_ref":"Q03","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q03-SP01","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Find position at t=6 s.","bucket":"B03","source_ref":"Q03","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q03-SP02","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Find displacement components and distance.","bucket":"B03","source_ref":"Q03","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q03-SP03","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Sketch start/end/direction; explain negative component.","bucket":"B03","source_ref":"Q03","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q04-FULL","kind":"source_question_full","text":"At t = 0, A is at x = 0 m and B is at x = 30 m on an east–west line. A travels east at 8 m/s and B travels east at 5 m/s. (a) Find A's velocity relative to B, stating the direction. (b) When and where does A catch B? (c) What is B's velocity relative to A?","bucket":"B05","source_ref":"Q04","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q04-D01","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"A x0=0 m","bucket":"B05","source_ref":"Q04","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q04-D02","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"B x0=30 m","bucket":"B05","source_ref":"Q04","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q04-D03","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"A east 8 m/s","bucket":"B05","source_ref":"Q04","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q04-D04","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"B east 5 m/s","bucket":"B05","source_ref":"Q04","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q04-D05","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"t=0 simultaneous","bucket":"B05","source_ref":"Q04","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q04-SP01","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Find A relative B.","bucket":"B05","source_ref":"Q04","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q04-SP02","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Find catch time and position.","bucket":"B05","source_ref":"Q04","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q04-SP03","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Find B relative A.","bucket":"B05","source_ref":"Q04","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q05-FULL","kind":"source_question_full","text":"At t = 0, A is at x = 0 m travelling east at 6 m/s and B is at x = 50 m travelling west at 4 m/s. (a) Find the time and position of meeting. (b) Give the velocity of A relative to B and the velocity of B relative to A. Explain each sign.","bucket":"B05","source_ref":"Q05","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q05-D01","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"A x0=0 m","bucket":"B05","source_ref":"Q05","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q05-D02","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"A east 6 m/s","bucket":"B05","source_ref":"Q05","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q05-D03","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"B x0=50 m","bucket":"B05","source_ref":"Q05","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q05-D04","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"B west 4 m/s","bucket":"B05","source_ref":"Q05","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q05-D05","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"t=0 simultaneous","bucket":"B05","source_ref":"Q05","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q05-SP01","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Find meeting time and position.","bucket":"B05","source_ref":"Q05","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q05-SP02","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Find A/B and B/A and explain signs.","bucket":"B05","source_ref":"Q05","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q06-FULL","kind":"source_question_full","text":"A and B start from the same point at t = 0. A travels east at 3 m/s; B travels north at 4 m/s. (a) Find A's velocity relative to B as components and magnitude. (b) Find their separation after 10 s. (c) Reverse the observer and explain what changes and what remains the same.","bucket":"B06","source_ref":"Q06","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q06-D01","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"same initial point","bucket":"B06","source_ref":"Q06","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q06-D02","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"A east 3 m/s","bucket":"B06","source_ref":"Q06","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q06-D03","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"B north 4 m/s","bucket":"B06","source_ref":"Q06","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q06-D04","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"t=0 simultaneous","bucket":"B06","source_ref":"Q06","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q06-D05","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"separation requested at 10 s","bucket":"B06","source_ref":"Q06","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q06-SP01","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Find A/B components and magnitude.","bucket":"B06","source_ref":"Q06","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q06-SP02","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Find separation after 10 s.","bucket":"B06","source_ref":"Q06","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q06-SP03","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Reverse observer and explain change/invariant.","bucket":"B06","source_ref":"Q06","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q07-FULL","kind":"source_question_full","text":"At t = 0, A is at (0, 0) m with velocity (2, 1) m/s. B is at (10, 0) m with velocity (0, 2) m/s. Do they meet? Show the x-coordinate and y-coordinate conditions using the same time. If they meet, give that time and position.","bucket":"B07","source_ref":"Q07","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q07-D01","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"A r0=(0,0) m","bucket":"B07","source_ref":"Q07","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q07-D02","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"A v=(2,1) m/s","bucket":"B07","source_ref":"Q07","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q07-D03","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"B r0=(10,0) m","bucket":"B07","source_ref":"Q07","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q07-D04","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"B v=(0,2) m/s","bucket":"B07","source_ref":"Q07","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q07-D05","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"t=0 simultaneous","bucket":"B07","source_ref":"Q07","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q07-SP01","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Test both coordinate equalities with same time; if meeting, give time/position.","bucket":"B07","source_ref":"Q07","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q08-FULL","kind":"source_question_full","text":"At t = 0, A is at (0, 0) m with velocity (2, 0) m/s. B is at (6, −4) m with velocity (0, 2) m/s. (a) Do they meet? Test both coordinates. (b) Explain why crossing paths need not mean collision. (c) As labelled enrichment, find their closest separation for t ≥ 0 using a table and/or completing a square, without calculus.","bucket":"B07","source_ref":"Q08","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q08-D01","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"A r0=(0,0) m","bucket":"B07","source_ref":"Q08","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q08-D02","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"A v=(2,0) m/s","bucket":"B07","source_ref":"Q08","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q08-D03","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"B r0=(6,-4) m","bucket":"B07","source_ref":"Q08","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q08-D04","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"B v=(0,2) m/s","bucket":"B07","source_ref":"Q08","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q08-D05","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"t>=0 for closest approach","bucket":"B07","source_ref":"Q08","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q08-SP01","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Do they meet?","bucket":"B07","source_ref":"Q08","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q08-SP02","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Explain path crossing versus collision.","bucket":"B07","source_ref":"Q08","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q08-SP03","kind":"source_subpart","text":"En