":"B08","source_ref":"Q09","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q09-SP03","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Find path length and label frames.","bucket":"B08","source_ref":"Q09","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q10-FULL","kind":"source_question_full","text":"Rain has ground-frame velocity (0, −6) m/s. An observer travels east with ground-frame velocity (8, 0) m/s. (a) Find the rain's velocity relative to the observer as components and magnitude. (b) Draw the ground and observer-frame arrows. (c) Explain which way the rain moves horizontally relative to the observer. An exact angle is not required.","bucket":"B08","source_ref":"Q10","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q10-D01","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"rain/ground=(0,-6) m/s","bucket":"B08","source_ref":"Q10","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q10-D02","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"observer/ground=(8,0) m/s","bucket":"B08","source_ref":"Q10","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q10-D03","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"observer travels east","bucket":"B08","source_ref":"Q10","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q10-D04","kind":"source_datum_or_condition","text":"exact angle not required","bucket":"B08","source_ref":"Q10","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q10-SP01","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Find rain/observer components/magnitude.","bucket":"B08","source_ref":"Q10","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q10-SP02","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Draw ground/observer arrows.","bucket":"B08","source_ref":"Q10","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q10-SP03","kind":"source_subpart","text":"Explain horizontal direction.","bucket":"B08","source_ref":"Q10","required":true,"notes":""},{"atom_id":"SRC-Q11-FULL","kind":"source_question_full","text":"A cyclist travels east at 36 km/h and a walker travels east at 2 m/s. They are at the same point at t = 0. (a) Convert the cyclist's speed to m/s. (b) Find the cyclist's